{
  "$comment": "Canvas-only values: things Iter's tokens.json does not hold because macOS draws them (window chrome, glass, materials, system control fills, map placeholder) plus the canvas furniture around artboards (labels, notes, specimen frames). Edit here, then run `node Design/paper/tools/gen-tokens.mjs`. A colour is {light, dark}; each side is a CSS colour string or {\"from\": \"<tokens.json colour name>\", \"alpha\": 0.16} which gen-tokens resolves from tokens.json (so a retheme flows through). Keys starting with 'shadow/' are box-shadow strings (not sent to Paper). Values are chosen to match macOS 26 (Tahoe) light and dark appearance. Materials are drawn translucent with a backdrop blur (materialSurface() in lib/chrome.mjs); backdrop-filter support in Paper is unconfirmed, so the fill opacity alone must read acceptably: material fills are 92-96% opaque.",
  "$lineHeightsComment": "Line heights are not in tokens.json. These are Apple's default macOS leading per text style (Human Interface Guidelines, 'Typography', macOS built-in text styles table: size/leading in points).",
  "lineHeights": {
    "largeTitle": {
      "size": 26,
      "lineHeight": 32
    },
    "title": {
      "size": 22,
      "lineHeight": 26
    },
    "title2": {
      "size": 17,
      "lineHeight": 22
    },
    "title3": {
      "size": 15,
      "lineHeight": 20
    },
    "headline": {
      "size": 13,
      "lineHeight": 16
    },
    "body": {
      "size": 13,
      "lineHeight": 16
    },
    "callout": {
      "size": 12,
      "lineHeight": 15
    },
    "subheadline": {
      "size": 11,
      "lineHeight": 14
    },
    "footnote": {
      "size": 10,
      "lineHeight": 13
    },
    "caption": {
      "size": 10,
      "lineHeight": 13
    }
  },
  "fontFamilies": {
    "sans": "\"SF Pro\", \"SF Pro Text\", -apple-system, system-ui, sans-serif",
    "serif": "\"New York\", ui-serif, serif"
  },
